      answer: "b", explanation: "Brown algae characteristically store mannitol and laminarin, so ordinary starch cannot be assigned universally to all algae. The printed Laminarian oil wording is corrected because laminarin is a carbohydrate rather than an oil.", sectionId: "boundary-three-algal-groups", source: { document: "quick-revision", page: 110 }, cognitive: "understanding"
